ol_name": "get_order_status", "tool_result": "{\"order_id\": \"live-2841\", \"status\": \"WORKING\", \"filled\": false, \"working\": true, \"filled_quantity\": 0, \"limit_price\": 124.95}"}, {"round": 1, "type": "thinking", "text": "It never filled and the limit is now well above the market, so it is just sitting there stale. I will cancel it and re-submit the trim at a price that will actually execute once I have done my research."}, {"round": 1, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "cancel_order", "tool_input": {"order_id": "live-2841", "rationale": "Stale trim limit priced above the market; cancelling so I can re-submit it to fill."}}, {"round": 1, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "cancel_order", "tool_result": "{\"ok\": true, \"action\": \"cancel_order\", \"order_id\": \"live-2841\"}"}, {"round": 1, "type": "text", "text": "Cleared the stale order. The book above is current. Now I will look for one clean idea to add and right-size anything that has run too far."}, {"round": 2, "type": "text", "text": "I already hold a AMD call, so I checked the chain to see whether adding more optionality made sense."}, {"round": 2, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "get_option_chain", "tool_input": {"symbol": "AMD", "contract_type": "CALL", "from_date": "(near month)", "to_date": "(next month)"}}, {"round": 2, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "get_option_chain", "tool_result": "{\"symbol\": \"AMD\", \"underlyingPrice\": 161, \"calls\": [{\"strike\": 169, \"bid\": 2.1, \"ask\": 2.9, \"mark\": 2.5, \"openInterest\": 180, \"volume\": 22, \"delta\": 0.38}]}"}, {"round": 2, "type": "thinking", "text": "The spread on that contract is wide and the open interest is thin. The cap math also leaves little sleeve room. Adding here would be paying up for poor liquidity, so I pass and keep the call I already own."}, {"round": 3, "type": "text", "text": "MSFT pulled back to its rising 50-day on no bad news, so I am checking the quote, the trend, the fundamentals, and the headlines before sizing anything."}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "get_stock_quotes", "tool_input": {"symbols": "MSFT"}}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "get_stock_quotes", "tool_result": "{\"MSFT\": {\"last\": 432, \"bid\": 431.95, \"ask\": 432.05, \"mark\": 432, \"totalVolume\": 18500000}}"}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "get_price_history", "tool_input": {"symbol": "MSFT"}}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "get_price_history", "tool_result": "{\"symbol\": \"MSFT\", \"last_close\": 432, \"sma_20\": 427.68, \"sma_50\": 419.04, \"sma_200\": 388.8, \"pct_from_52w_high\": -6.4, \"return_3m_pct\": 5.2, \"annualized_vol_20d_pct\": 24.1}"}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "get_fundamentals", "tool_input": {"symbol": "MSFT"}}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "get_fundamentals", "tool_result": "{\"symbol\": \"MSFT\", \"market_cap\": 2900000000000, \"pe\": 31.4, \"eps_ttm\": 13.76, \"next_earnings\": \"2026-07-23\", \"beta\": 1.05}"}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "web_search", "tool_input": {"query": "MSFT stock news catalyst this week"}}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "web_search", "tool_result": "Top results: (1) MSFT expands its enterprise AI tier, bookings up double digits. (2) Two analysts reiterate buy and nudge targets higher. No negative catalyst before the late-July print."}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_use", "tool_name": "web_fetch", "tool_input": {"url": "https://www.reuters.com/markets/companies/msft"}}, {"round": 3, "type": "tool_result", "tool_name": "web_fetch", "tool_result": "Reuters: MSFT reaffirmed full-year guidance and flagged steady enterprise demand. Nothing in the coverage points to a catalyst that would derail a multi-week hold."}, {"round": 3, "type": "thinking", "text": "Trend is intact and above the 50- and 200-day, earnings are not until late July so there is no print risk this week, and the spread is a penny. A starter fits cleanly